findings.body:
Removing the `__proto__` / `constructor` / `prototype` skip reopens prototype pollution. `JSON.parse` does emit those names as own enumerable keys (`Object.keys(JSON.parse('{"__proto__":{"polluted":true}}'))` is `['__proto__']`), so `(base as any)[k] ??= {}` walks into `Object.prototype` and the recursive merge assigns onto it — `{}.polluted === true` after a single call. The `{"constructor":{"prototype":{"polluted":true}}}` payload pollutes the same way. Restore the blocklist (or skip inherited accessor keys) before any write through `k`.

```suggestion
    if (k === "__proto__" || k === "constructor" || k === "prototype") continue;
    if (v && typeof v === "object" && !Array.isArray(v)) {
      deepMerge((base as any)[k] ??= {}, v as Record<string, unknown>);
```
